{{/*
  claim-clear — pre-close cleanup block that strips the `in-flight` label,
  unsets the two pure-liveness claim metadata keys (`claimed_by`,
  `claim_heartbeat_at`), and promotes `claimed_at` into `work_started_at`
  before unsetting it (mitto-v3en: `claimed_at` is the only available
  work-start signal on a closed bead — `bd` exposes no `started_at` field —
  so deleting it unconditionally, as this fragment used to do, destroyed
  that signal). Invoked immediately BEFORE every `bd close` written by an
  L2 driver's Done branch or the L1 orchestrator's terminal-label sweep —
  otherwise closed beads carry ghost claims into archives / JIRA sync
  (mitto-ial bead description note).

  Usage — one line above the `bd close` command:

      {{ template "beads-issues/shared/claim-clear" (dict
          "Target" $target
      ) }}
      bd close {{ $target }} --reason "..."

  Parameters:
    Target — the resolved bead ID. Required; empty string skips the block
             (there is no bead to clean up).

  Idempotency: `--remove-label` on a bead that does not carry the label,
  and `--unset-metadata` on a key that is not set, are both no-ops in
  `bd`, so this template is safe to invoke even when the driver never
  actually claimed the bead (e.g. a Done branch reached on the very
  first iteration before Step 0 wrote the claim). The `work_started_at`
  promotion is additionally guarded on absence — a bead re-claimed after
  being reaped (Step 2R) keeps the earliest recorded start time rather
  than having it overwritten on a later close.
*/}}
{{- if .Target }}
Clear the passive claim before closing (see mitto-ial — ghost claims must
not survive into archives). Promote `claimed_at` into `work_started_at`
first, guarded on `work_started_at` being absent (earliest-start
semantics), since `claimed_at` carries no liveness meaning but is the only
work-start signal available (mitto-v3en):

```bash
started=$(bd show {{ .Target }} --json | jq -r '.[0].metadata.claimed_at // empty')
prior=$(bd show {{ .Target }} --json | jq -r '.[0].metadata.work_started_at // empty')
if [ -n "$started" ] && [ -z "$prior" ]; then
  bd update {{ .Target }} --remove-label in-flight \
    --unset-metadata claimed_by \
    --unset-metadata claimed_at \
    --unset-metadata claim_heartbeat_at \
    --set-metadata "work_started_at=$started"
else
  bd update {{ .Target }} --remove-label in-flight \
    --unset-metadata claimed_by \
    --unset-metadata claimed_at \
    --unset-metadata claim_heartbeat_at
fi
```
{{- end }}
